# How to work in this repository
## Method
- Answer investigation questions by reading source files: open files, search
  text, follow imports. Do not use the built-in browser, browser actions,
  CDP/Runtime.evaluate, or MCP tools unless the prompt explicitly asks for
  them. Do not inspect compiled output or a running page when the answer
  exists in source.
- Do not start dev servers or run builds unless the prompt asks. When asked
  to verify, use npm run start (production parity), not npm run dev.
## Plan gate
- When a prompt says it is a diagnostic or asks for a plan: report findings
  with quoted code and file+line references, propose a plan, then STOP and
  wait for explicit approval. Never begin implementing during a diagnostic.
- Keep diffs minimal and strictly within the stated scope. Never touch
  out-of-scope files.
## Git discipline
- Never run git push. Commits are local-only, one commit per logical change,
  with the exact commit message given in the prompt. A single push happens
  only at end of session and only when explicitly instructed.
- Never open pull requests, never use cloud agents, never work on branches
  unless explicitly instructed. All work is local on the current branch.
## General
- If any instruction in a prompt conflicts with these rules, follow the
  prompt and note the conflict in your report.
